      "value": "**We don't have custom fonts in VRChat.** Its all the same font, depending on which part of the UI you're looking at. Nameplate is Noto Sans I think? Most of the UI is either Dosis or Noto Sans. Anyhow.\nWhat you're talking about is Unicode code points or alternate characters, like this: タッパー, or віртуальна реальність, or 가상 현실 헤드셋. I didn't change fonts there!\nUnicode's mapping of these codepoints allows a single font to account for the characters/letters of many different languages for their names.\nObviously, we want to have these available as much as possible. We have some filtering for non-useful codepoints (invisible characters, mostly). \nWhat it seems like you're asking is for us to limit names to Latin characters (ABCabc123, etc), which... well, no, we're not going to do. That excludes many people around the world from using the name they want to, in the language they want to use.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
