      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: they're probably talking about unicode characters that have a different unicode ID but look the exact same, like a and а for example. They can't be told apart but they still have a different unicode, so that can be abused to impersonate people. Here's a list of some of them: https://gist.github.com/StevenACoffman/a5f6f682d94e38ed804182dc2693ed4b\nWhile some are just altered for prenounciation like e and é, others look the exact same and can't be told apart even if you look very closely",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
